From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krane <chris@krane.dev>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 21:50:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] idle: also hold a logind idle lock while Keep awake is on

Hyprland ignores a layer-surface idle inhibitor while the layer's alpha
is zero, which happens during its fade-in and whenever a fullscreen
window covers the monitor. hypridle then locked the session even with
Keep awake on. Also take a systemd-inhibit idle lock, which hypridle
honours independently of Wayland surface state.

Drop when Hyprland counts layer-surface inhibitors regardless of alpha.
---
 dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml
--- a/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml
+++ b/dots/.config/quickshell/ii/services/Idle.qml
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 import qs.modules.common
 import QtQuick
 import Quickshell
+import Quickshell.Io
 import Quickshell.Wayland
 
 /**
@@ -45,6 +46,18 @@
         }
     }
 
+    // Hyprland ignores a layer-surface inhibitor while the layer's alpha is
+    // zero: during its fade-in and whenever a fullscreen window covers the
+    // monitor. hypridle then locks anyway. Also hold a logind idle inhibitor
+    // lock, which hypridle honours on its own. `cat` waits on stdin, so it
+    // exits and frees the lock as soon as Quickshell stops the process or dies.
+    Process {
+        running: root.inhibit
+        stdinEnabled: true
+        command: ["systemd-inhibit", "--what=idle", "--mode=block",
+            "--who=Quickshell", "--why=Keep awake", "cat"]
+    }
+
     IdleInhibitor {
         id: idleInhibitor
         window: PanelWindow {
